module engine where

-- floor-axioms.fenel — the Layer-1 floor-axiom WITNESSES (floor-kernel
-- Phase 1). Sibling of floor-isos.fenel: that file carries the ADT↔floor
-- isos (ISO-2/4/5); THIS file carries the Boolean/lattice ALGEBRA —
-- `design/floor-kernel.md` §3.2's data-fragment axiom instances, each as
-- (i) a derivation witness where the law is a rewrite (`∖ = ∩ ∘ ¬`,
-- De Morgan, `¬¬`, `⊥ = ∪∅`, `⊤ = ∩∅`, enum = ∪-of-singletons) and (ii) an
-- EQUALITY CLAIM AS DATA (`FloorLawClaim`) whose denotational truth the
-- decide substrate itself judges — mutual subset via the trio
-- (`floorLawEqBySubset`) + the judgment-iso face, symmetric-difference
-- emptiness via `decideEmpty` (`floorLawEqByEmpty`, which rides the D′
-- search fall-through and decides MORE — the §3.3 precision story made
-- measurable). The prover certifying its own algebra.
--
-- THE FENCED LEDGER IS THE DELIVERABLE, not a failure: where the shipped
-- deciders return `Nothing` on a true law (the complement fences), the
-- verdict is RECORDED (floor-axioms.test.ts pins the decided-vs-fenced
-- table) and feeds Phase 2 (kernel-axiom audit / TCB ledger) and Phase 3
-- (¬-over-arrows unfencing). Tri discipline: a fenced Nothing is never
-- license to guess; a false `Just` is a decider bug (three were found and
-- fixed by this phase's probe — subsetAllArm's compound blanket-refutation,
-- the enum-⊆-∪ split false-refutation, subsetSome's all-refuted collapse;
-- see set-algebra-deciders.fenel "floor-kernel Phase 1 SOUNDNESS FIX").
--
-- Se*-LEVEL AUTHORING: the canonical `$tag` Se* constructors are PLAIN
-- (`SeUnion { branches = … }`) — a `.fenel` body authors set expressions
-- directly; the `$`-key barrier does not bite here (it bites only legacy
-- `$`-keyed shapes). No TraversalType marshal is needed for lattice laws.
--
-- SeCtor DECOMPOSITION LEVEL-CHECK VERDICT (brief task 4, §6.1
-- `SeCtor c fs ≅ {c} ∩ ⟦fs⟧`): PRESENTATIONAL ONLY at the Se* level — no
-- executable witness ships here. The naive rewrite target
-- `SeIntersect [SeCtor c [], SeCtor "" fs]` exists syntactically, but both
-- operands are OUTSIDE the deciders' canonical-term domain (8μ.1a assumes
-- field-COMPLETE projections): the membership face treats ctor "" as
-- tag-agnostic while the subset face treats it as a regular distinct tag
-- (⇒ false `Just false` on the fwd inclusion), and a tag-only `SeCtor c []`
-- for a non-nullary c gets a vacuous-fieldwise false `Just true`
-- (`P{} ⊆ P{f:{1}}`). The tag-singleton `{c}` is a component of the VALUE's
-- tag field, not a freestanding Se* former — exactly ISO-2's variant-level
-- reading, which already carries the witness (floor-isos.fenel). Ledgered
-- as Phase-2 input: the 8μ.1a canonical-domain assumption must be stated
-- as an explicit side-condition in the TCB ledger.
--
-- Parser-fence discipline (the floor-isos header): single-line arms,
-- comment-free in-chain, head/tail accumulator folds, per-decl token cap,
-- helpers split liberally. PLUS one discovered here (Phase-1 surprise): a
-- record-literal field whose value is an INLINE LIST LITERAL
-- (`{ branches = [l, …] }`) parses as an APPLICATION (`branches [l, …]`)
-- in nested positions (case arms, record-field values) — only a top-level
-- decl RHS reads it as a binding. Hence the floorOne/floorPair appendItem
-- builders below (the jopSubset `appendItem s (appendItem t [])` idiom,
-- now named): NEVER inline a multi-element list literal as a record field.

-- FloorLawClaim — a lattice-law equality claim as first-class data: a law
-- `name` + the two Se* sides whose denotational equality the trio judges.
@entity
@label "FloorLawClaim"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — a Layer-1 lattice-law equality claim as data: `lhs ≅ rhs` over canonical Se* SetExprs (design/floor-kernel.md §3.2). Built by the law builders (lawDiffDef / lawDeMorganIntersect / …); judged by floorLawVerdicts (mutual subset + symmetric-difference emptiness through the shipped trio). The decided-vs-fenced ledger over these claims is Phase 1's deliverable and Phase 2/3's input."
FloorLawClaim = FloorLawClaim name: String lhs: SetExpr rhs: SetExpr

-- ===========================================================================
-- Derivation witnesses — Layer-1 formers rewritten over Layer 0
-- (`design/floor-kernel.md` §1 Layer-1 table). WITNESS, not demolition: the
-- derived formers stay efficient reps; each fn names the definitional
-- rewrite, fwd total on the matching former (pass-through otherwise), bwd
-- PARTIAL (Nothing where the floor term has no derived-former preimage —
-- the floor-isos discipline).
-- ===========================================================================

-- floorOne / floorPair — order-explicit list builders (appendItem appends to
-- the END, so floorPair x y = [x, y]). The parser-limitation workaround named:
-- a record field can carry a CALL result but not an inline list literal.
@label "floor-axioms: floorOne"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the singleton list [x] via appendItem (the record-field inline-list-literal parser limitation workaround; see the file header). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorOne : (x: a) -> List a
floorOne x =
  appendItem x []

@label "floor-axioms: floorPair"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the two-element list [x, y] via appendItem chaining, order-explicit (appendItem appends to the END). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorPair : (x: a) -> (y: a) -> List a
floorPair x y =
  appendItem y (appendItem x [])

@label "Diff to floor"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `∖ = ∩ ∘ ¬` derivation witness (fwd): rewrite `SeDiff a b` to its Layer-0 definition `SeIntersect [a, SeComplement b]` (§3.2 `∖ = ∩ ∘ ¬`). Identity on values — the iso is denotational; the equality claim is lawDiffDef. Non-diff input passes through unchanged."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "axiom" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
diffToFloor : (s: a) -> a
diffToFloor s =
  case s of
    SeDiff { left = l, right = r } -> SeIntersect { branches = floorPair l (SeComplement { inner = r }) }
    other -> other

@label "Floor to diff"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `∖ = ∩ ∘ ¬` derivation witness (bwd, partial): a binary `SeIntersect [a, SeComplement b]` merges back to `SeDiff a b`; any other shape ⇒ Nothing (no diff preimage). Left-inverse of diffToFloor (the round-trip law is discharged in the Phase-1 harness)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "axiom" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
floorToDiff : (s: a) -> Maybe a
floorToDiff s =
  case s of
    SeIntersect { branches = bs } -> floorToDiffBranches bs
    other -> Nothing

@label "floor-axioms: floorToDiffBranches"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — floorToDiff helper: exactly two branches with the second a SeComplement ⇒ Just (SeDiff first inner); else Nothing. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorToDiffBranches : (bs: List a) -> Maybe a
floorToDiffBranches bs =
  if not (eq (length bs) 2)
  then Nothing
  else case head bs of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just a ->
      case floorToDiffSecond (tail bs) of
        Nothing -> Nothing
        Just r -> Just (SeDiff { left = a, right = r })

@label "floor-axioms: floorToDiffSecond"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — floorToDiff helper: the second branch must be a SeComplement; returns its inner. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorToDiffSecond : (mRest: a) -> Maybe b
floorToDiffSecond mRest =
  case mRest of
    Nothing -> Nothing
    Just rest ->
      case head rest of
        Nothing -> Nothing
        Just second ->
          case second of
            SeComplement { inner = i } -> Just i
            other -> Nothing

@label "Intersect to neg-union"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the De Morgan derivation witness (fwd): rewrite `SeIntersect bs` to the `{¬, ∪}`-basis form `SeComplement (SeUnion [¬b …])` (§2.1 — the Boolean collapse, DATA-FRAGMENT-scoped: above the data fragment ∩ is independent because ¬ fences). The equality claim is lawDeMorganIntersect. Non-intersect input passes through unchanged."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "axiom" "de-morgan" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
intersectToNegUnion : (s: a) -> a
intersectToNegUnion s =
  case s of
    SeIntersect { branches = bs } -> SeComplement { inner = SeUnion { branches = floorComplementEach bs } }
    other -> other

@label "Neg-union to intersect"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the De Morgan derivation witness (bwd, partial): `SeComplement (SeUnion bs)` with EVERY branch a SeComplement merges back to `SeIntersect [inner …]`; any other shape ⇒ Nothing. Left-inverse of intersectToNegUnion."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "axiom" "de-morgan" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
negUnionToIntersect : (s: a) -> Maybe a
negUnionToIntersect s =
  case s of
    SeComplement { inner = i } -> negUnionInner i
    other -> Nothing

@label "floor-axioms: negUnionInner"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — negUnionToIntersect helper: the complement's inner must be a SeUnion; un-complement every branch. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
negUnionInner : (i: a) -> Maybe a
negUnionInner i =
  case i of
    SeUnion { branches = bs } ->
      case floorUncomplementEach bs of
        Nothing -> Nothing
        Just inners -> Just (SeIntersect { branches = inners })
    other -> Nothing

@label "Eliminate double complement"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `¬¬A = A` (classical involution) derivation witness: `SeComplement (SeComplement x)` rewrites to `x` (§3.2; data-fragment classicality — design/floor-kernel.md §4). The equality claim is lawDoubleComplement. Any other shape passes through unchanged."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "axiom" "complement" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
elimDoubleComplement : (s: a) -> a
elimDoubleComplement s =
  case s of
    SeComplement { inner = i } -> elimDoubleComplementInner s i
    other -> other

@label "floor-axioms: elimDoubleComplementInner"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — elimDoubleComplement helper: inner also a complement ⇒ its inner; else the original. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
elimDoubleComplementInner : (orig: a) -> (i: a) -> a
elimDoubleComplementInner orig i =
  case i of
    SeComplement { inner = x } -> x
    other -> orig

@label "Enum to singleton union"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the enum-decomposition derivation witness (fwd): `SeEnum [v, w, …]` rewrites to the finite `∪` of singletons `SeUnion [SeEnum [v], SeEnum [w], …]` (§1 Layer-1: SeEnum is derived; the singletons `{v}` are the Layer-0 atoms). The equality claim is lawEnumDecomposition. Non-enum input passes through unchanged."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "axiom" "enum" "singleton" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
enumToSingletonUnion : (s: a) -> a
enumToSingletonUnion s =
  case s of
    SeEnum { values = vs } -> SeUnion { branches = floorSingletonEach vs }
    other -> other

@label "Singleton union to enum"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the enum-decomposition derivation witness (bwd, partial): a `SeUnion` whose branches are ALL enums merges their value lists back into one `SeEnum` (order-preserving concat); any non-enum branch ⇒ Nothing (no enum preimage — the union genuinely mixes formers). Left-inverse of enumToSingletonUnion."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "axiom" "enum" "singleton" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
singletonUnionToEnum : (s: a) -> Maybe a
singletonUnionToEnum s =
  case s of
    SeUnion { branches = bs } -> floorEnumMergeFold bs []
    other -> Nothing

@label "None to empty union"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `⊥ = ∪∅` derivation witness: `SeNone` rewrites to the nullary join `SeUnion []` (§3.2 `∪∅ = ⊥`). The equality claim is lawNullaryUnion. Any other shape passes through unchanged."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "axiom" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
noneToEmptyUnion : (s: a) -> a
noneToEmptyUnion s =
  case s of
    SeNone ->
      let none = []
      SeUnion { branches = none }
    other -> other

@label "All to empty intersect"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `⊤ = ∩∅` derivation witness: `SeAll` rewrites to the nullary meet `SeIntersect []` (§3.2 `∩∅ = ⊤`). The equality claim is lawNullaryIntersect. Any other shape passes through unchanged."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "axiom" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
allToEmptyIntersect : (s: a) -> a
allToEmptyIntersect s =
  case s of
    SeAll ->
      let none = []
      SeIntersect { branches = none }
    other -> other

-- ── fold helpers (the floor-isos accumulator pattern) ──────────────────────

@label "floor-axioms: complementEach"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — wrap every branch in SeComplement (order-preserving). Internal helper to intersectToNegUnion."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorComplementEach : (branches: List a) -> List a
floorComplementEach branches =
  floorComplementEachAcc branches []

@label "floor-axioms: complementEachAcc"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — accumulator fold for floorComplementEach. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorComplementEachAcc : (branches: List a) -> (acc: List a) -> List a
floorComplementEachAcc branches acc =
  case head branches of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just b ->
      let acc2 = appendItem (SeComplement { inner = b }) acc
      case tail branches of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> floorComplementEachAcc rest acc2

@label "floor-axioms: uncomplementEach"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — unwrap every branch's SeComplement (Just inners), Nothing the moment a branch is not a complement. Internal helper to negUnionToIntersect."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorUncomplementEach : (branches: List a) -> Maybe (List a)
floorUncomplementEach branches =
  floorUncomplementEachAcc branches []

@label "floor-axioms: uncomplementEachAcc"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — accumulator fold for floorUncomplementEach (Nothing on a non-complement branch). Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorUncomplementEachAcc : (branches: List a) -> (acc: List a) -> Maybe (List a)
floorUncomplementEachAcc branches acc =
  case head branches of
    Nothing -> Just acc
    Just b ->
      case b of
        SeComplement { inner = i } ->
          let acc2 = appendItem i acc
          case tail branches of
            Nothing -> Just acc2
            Just rest -> floorUncomplementEachAcc rest acc2
        other -> Nothing

@label "floor-axioms: singletonEach"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — one singleton SeEnum per value (order-preserving). Internal helper to enumToSingletonUnion."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorSingletonEach : (values: List a) -> List b
floorSingletonEach values =
  floorSingletonEachAcc values []

@label "floor-axioms: singletonEachAcc"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — accumulator fold for floorSingletonEach. Internal helper."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorSingletonEachAcc : (values: List a) -> (acc: List b) -> List b
floorSingletonEachAcc values acc =
  case head values of
    Nothing -> acc
    Just v ->
      let acc2 = appendItem (SeEnum { values = floorOne v }) acc
      case tail values of
        Nothing -> acc2
        Just rest -> floorSingletonEachAcc rest acc2

@label "floor-axioms: enumMergeFold"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — concat every all-enum branch's values into one SeEnum (Nothing on a non-enum branch). Internal helper to singletonUnionToEnum."
@tags "engine" "internal" "set-algebra" "floor" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
@category "engine-internal"
floorEnumMergeFold : (branches: List a) -> (acc: List b) -> Maybe c
floorEnumMergeFold branches acc =
  case head branches of
    Nothing -> Just (SeEnum { values = acc })
    Just b ->
      case b of
        SeEnum { values = bvs } ->
          let acc2 = concat acc bvs
          case tail branches of
            Nothing -> Just (SeEnum { values = acc2 })
            Just rest -> floorEnumMergeFold rest acc2
        other -> Nothing

-- ===========================================================================
-- The law claims as data — one builder per §3.2 data-fragment axiom
-- instance. Where a derivation witness exists, the rhs is BUILT BY the
-- witness (the claim literally asserts "the rewrite preserves denotation");
-- the axioms without a rewrite (excluded middle, non-contradiction) state
-- both sides directly.
-- ===========================================================================

@label "Law: diff definition"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `∖ = ∩ ∘ ¬` axiom instance over operands a, b: `SeDiff a b ≅ diffToFloor (SeDiff a b)` = `SeIntersect [a, ¬b]` (§3.2)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawDiffDef : (a: x) -> (b: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawDiffDef a b =
  let d = SeDiff { left = a, right = b }
  let floored = diffToFloor d
  FloorLawClaim { name = "diff-def", lhs = d, rhs = floored }

@label "Law: De Morgan (intersect)"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the De Morgan axiom instance over operands a, b: `SeIntersect [a,b] ≅ intersectToNegUnion (SeIntersect [a,b])` = `¬(¬a ∪ ¬b)` (§3.2; §2.1 data-fragment scope)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "de-morgan" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawDeMorganIntersect : (a: x) -> (b: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawDeMorganIntersect a b =
  let i = SeIntersect { branches = floorPair a b }
  let floored = intersectToNegUnion i
  FloorLawClaim { name = "de-morgan-intersect", lhs = i, rhs = floored }

@label "Law: double complement"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `¬¬A = A` axiom instance over operand a: `SeComplement (SeComplement a) ≅ a` (§3.2 classical involution)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "complement" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawDoubleComplement : (a: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawDoubleComplement a =
  let dc = SeComplement { inner = SeComplement { inner = a } }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "double-complement", lhs = dc, rhs = elimDoubleComplement dc }

@label "Law: excluded middle"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `A ∪ ¬A = ⊤` axiom instance over operand a (§3.2; the classical seam — expected to FENCE pre-Phase-3: ⊤ ⊆ A∪¬A needs classical ¬)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "complement" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawExcludedMiddle : (a: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawExcludedMiddle a =
  let u = SeUnion { branches = floorPair a (SeComplement { inner = a }) }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "excluded-middle", lhs = u, rhs = SeAll }

@label "Law: non-contradiction"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `A ∩ ¬A = ⊥` axiom instance over operand a (§3.2)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "complement" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawNonContradiction : (a: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawNonContradiction a =
  let i = SeIntersect { branches = floorPair a (SeComplement { inner = a }) }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "non-contradiction", lhs = i, rhs = SeNone }

@label "Law: nullary union"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `∪∅ = ⊥` axiom instance: `SeUnion [] ≅ SeNone` (§3.2; the Layer-1 ⊥ derivation)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawNullaryUnion : (unit: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawNullaryUnion unit =
  let none = []
  let u = SeUnion { branches = none }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "nullary-union", lhs = u, rhs = SeNone }

@label "Law: nullary intersect"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the `∩∅ = ⊤` axiom instance: `SeIntersect [] ≅ SeAll` (§3.2; the Layer-1 ⊤ derivation)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawNullaryIntersect : (unit: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawNullaryIntersect unit =
  let none = []
  let i = SeIntersect { branches = none }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "nullary-intersect", lhs = i, rhs = SeAll }

@label "Law: enum decomposition"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the enum-decomposition axiom instance over an enum e: `e ≅ enumToSingletonUnion e` (the finite ∪ of singletons — §1 Layer-1)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "enum" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawEnumDecomposition : (e: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawEnumDecomposition e =
  FloorLawClaim { name = "enum-decomposition", lhs = e, rhs = enumToSingletonUnion e }

@label "Law: idempotent union"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — lattice housekeeping: `A ∪ A ≅ A` (§3.2 idem of ∪)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "lattice" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawIdempotentUnion : (a: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawIdempotentUnion a =
  let u = SeUnion { branches = floorPair a a }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "idempotent-union", lhs = u, rhs = a }

@label "Law: idempotent intersect"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — lattice housekeeping: `A ∩ A ≅ A` (§3.2 idem of ∩)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "lattice" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawIdempotentIntersect : (a: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawIdempotentIntersect a =
  let i = SeIntersect { branches = floorPair a a }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "idempotent-intersect", lhs = i, rhs = a }

@label "Law: commutative union"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — lattice housekeeping: `A ∪ B ≅ B ∪ A` (§3.2 comm of ∪)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "lattice" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawCommutativeUnion : (a: x) -> (b: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawCommutativeUnion a b =
  let l = SeUnion { branches = floorPair a b }
  let r = SeUnion { branches = floorPair b a }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "commutative-union", lhs = l, rhs = r }

@label "Law: commutative intersect"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — lattice housekeeping: `A ∩ B ≅ B ∩ A` (§3.2 comm of ∩)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "lattice" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawCommutativeIntersect : (a: x) -> (b: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawCommutativeIntersect a b =
  let l = SeIntersect { branches = floorPair a b }
  let r = SeIntersect { branches = floorPair b a }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "commutative-intersect", lhs = l, rhs = r }

@label "Law: absorption (union)"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — lattice housekeeping: `A ∪ (A ∩ B) ≅ A` (§3.2 absorption)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "lattice" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawAbsorbUnion : (a: x) -> (b: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawAbsorbUnion a b =
  let meet = SeIntersect { branches = floorPair a b }
  let u = SeUnion { branches = floorPair a meet }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "absorb-union", lhs = u, rhs = a }

@label "Law: absorption (intersect)"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — lattice housekeeping: `A ∩ (A ∪ B) ≅ A` (§3.2 absorption)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "lattice" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
lawAbsorbIntersect : (a: x) -> (b: x) -> FloorLawClaim
lawAbsorbIntersect a b =
  let join = SeUnion { branches = floorPair a b }
  let i = SeIntersect { branches = floorPair a join }
  FloorLawClaim { name = "absorb-intersect", lhs = i, rhs = a }

-- ===========================================================================
-- The decision faces — the substrate judging its own algebra. Two routes
-- with DIFFERENT precision (the §3.3 tri-precision story, measured):
--   bySubset — mutual containment through the specialised subset rules;
--   byEmpty  — the judgment-iso face (`s ≅ t ⟺ empty(s∖t) ∧ empty(t∖s)`,
--              the Phase-2 decomposition), which rides decideEmpty's D′
--              bounded witness search and decides MORE on the finite
--              data fragment (e.g. De Morgan fwd).
-- Both are Tri-honest: Just true (theorem instance), Just false (refuted —
-- a decider bug or a wrong law; the harness STOPs on it), Nothing (fenced).
-- ===========================================================================

@label "Floor law eq (by subset)"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — denotational equality by MUTUAL SUBSET via the trio: mAnd (isSubset lhs rhs) (isSubset rhs lhs). Kleene-Tri: both Just true ⇒ Just true; either refuted ⇒ Just false; else Nothing (fenced)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "decide" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
floorLawEqBySubset : (lhs: a) -> (rhs: a) -> Maybe Bool
floorLawEqBySubset lhs rhs =
  mAnd (setAlgebraIsSubset lhs rhs) (setAlgebraIsSubset rhs lhs)

@label "Floor law eq (by emptiness)"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — denotational equality by SYMMETRIC-DIFFERENCE EMPTINESS: mAnd (decideEmpty (lhs∖rhs)) (decideEmpty (rhs∖lhs)) — the judgment-iso face (PropSubset s t ⟺ empty(s ∩ ¬t), decide-substrate Phase 2), riding decideEmpty's bounded witness-search fall-through. Decides strictly more than the subset face on the finite data fragment (the measured tri-precision gap the Phase-1 ledger records)."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "decide" "judgment" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
floorLawEqByEmpty : (lhs: a) -> (rhs: a) -> Maybe Bool
floorLawEqByEmpty lhs rhs =
  mAnd (setAlgebraDecideEmpty (SeDiff { left = lhs, right = rhs })) (setAlgebraDecideEmpty (SeDiff { left = rhs, right = lhs }))

@label "Floor law verdicts"
@description "floor-kernel Phase 1 — the full verdict record for one FloorLawClaim: per-direction subset verdicts (fwd = lhs ⊆ rhs, bwd = rhs ⊆ lhs), per-direction symmetric-difference emptiness (empFwd = empty(lhs∖rhs), empBwd = empty(rhs∖lhs)), and the two equality faces (bySubset / byEmpty, the mAnds). One call per ledger row; the Phase-1 harness pins the table."
@tags "engine" "set-algebra" "floor" "law" "decide" "floor-kernel" "phase-1"
floorLawVerdicts : (claim: FloorLawClaim) -> a
floorLawVerdicts claim =
  case claim of
    FloorLawClaim { lhs = l, rhs = r } ->
      let fwd = setAlgebraIsSubset l r
      let bwd = setAlgebraIsSubset r l
      let ef = setAlgebraDecideEmpty (SeDiff { left = l, right = r })
      let eb = setAlgebraDecideEmpty (SeDiff { left = r, right = l })
      { name = claim.name, fwd = fwd, bwd = bwd, empFwd = ef, empBwd = eb, bySubset = mAnd fwd bwd, byEmpty = mAnd ef eb }
